# What the MCP image does NOT need. Modelled on oregon-counties/.dockerignore (the sibling
# whose raw sources are also committed), with the snapshot question re-answered for THIS corpus.
#
# `.git` IS NOT HERE AND MUST NOT BE. It is a RUNTIME dependency: the toolkit's FTS cache key
# is `git rev-parse HEAD` plus a hash of `git status --porcelain`, and corpus_overview()
# shells out to `git log -1`. Exclude it and repo_state() collapses to a constant, so content
# changes stop invalidating the index -- silently, with everything still reporting healthy.

# THE SNAPSHOTS ARE A CI ARTIFACT, NOT A RUNTIME ONE. 4,563 committed files, 713 MB (1,672
# PDFs, 513 HTML, 2,281 extracted .txt, 38 docx, 54 json, 4 xml). The server never opens them.
# Verified by reading the code, not assumed (federal-reference excluded its snapshots and its
# citation module read one AT IMPORT, so the server died before answering a request):
#
#   * corpus_toolkit/mcp/ (framework, backends, server, responses, sdk) has no reference to
#     snapshots at all, and the modules it imports at run time -- config, plugins, remote,
#     repo's content_files/extract_fulltext/parse_frontmatter/repo_state, semantic.search --
#     only resolve the `snapshot_dir` PATH (config.py) and never open a file in it.
#     The readers are hash_snapshot(), grounding, validate/{provenance,extraction} and
#     sources/*: ingest and CI only.
#   * _meta/corpus.yml declares no plugins.citation_module, snapshot_slice_module,
#     semantic_search_module or tools_module, so no src/ file is imported by the server.
#     src/ is the ingester, which reads snapshots offline.
#   * tests/test_image.py rebuilds the image's context from this file, with no snapshots, and
#     runs the framework over it.
# Re-run that test if corpus.yml ever gains a plugin line.
#
# Consequence: `corpus-verify-provenance` cannot run INSIDE the container. It is a CI gate;
# run it against a checkout.
#
# NOT free, and the image does not shrink as much as the line suggests: the shallow clone's
# .git still holds every snapshot blob (479 MB packed, measured), because `.git` must stay.
# This line removes the 713 MB WORKING-TREE copy: context 798 MB -> 85 MB excluding .git.
_meta/snapshots/

# Rebuilt on demand inside the image by the Dockerfile's ensure_index step. Copying a
# host-built index in would ship one keyed to the host's repo state.
_meta/.cache/

# Mounted at runtime from the host, not copied. The artifact is built out of band on a GPU
# machine and arrives by platform-deploy's reconcile loop; a git-clone build cannot see it
# (it is untracked) and COPYing it would put the vectors in an image that reads a bind mount.
_meta/embeddings/

# Generated at deploy time by the pages workflow; never needed at runtime.
site/

# Never inputs to the server.
.github/
.obsidian/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
